{"plan_objective_id": 1, "updated_plan_objective_json": "{
  "id": 1,
  "objective": "Find measured thermal conductivity of as-built LPBF AlSi10Mg as a function of temperature (room temp to solidus), including laser flash diffusivity measurements, and heat treatment effects",
  "rationale": "Part (a) - found Butler 2021, Azizi 2023, Selo 2020. Butler measured at room temp using electrical resistivity method (not laser flash over temperature). Azizi used flash diffusivity. Key values: as-built 103-136 W/m-K at room temp depending on direction/energy density; heat treatment increases to 173-192 W/m-K. No temperature-dependent data from RT to solidus found in LPBF-specific papers.",
  "status": "completed",
  "result": "As-built LPBF AlSi10Mg: 103-136 W/m-K at RT (anisotropic); heat treatment (300°C/2h) increases to 173 W/m-K isotropic. Zero-porosity extrapolation: 143.9 as-built, 191.5 heat-treated. Heat treatment increases k by 18-41% (Butler), 44% (Selo T6). No temperature-dependent LPBF-specific data found from RT to solidus - cast AlSi10Mg data would be needed for temperature dependence.",
  "evaluation": "Found the best available data from Butler 2021 and Selo 2020. Temperature-dependent data from RT to solidus specifically for LPBF AlSi10Mg is sparse."
}"}

{"plan_objective_id": 3, "updated_plan_objective_json": "{
  "id": 3,
  "objective": "Find dynamic viscosity of liquid Al and liquid Al-Si alloys vs temperature with Arrhenius parameters and reference correlations",
  "rationale": "Found Assael 2012 with eutectic Al+Si reference correlation and recommended values table. Have Betzou data for Al-7Si and Al-20Si Arrhenius parameters.",
  "status": "completed",
  "result": "Assael 2012: eutectic Al+Si viscosity: log10(η/mPa·s) = 0.8022 + 658.34/T, 860-1275K, 7.7% 2σ. Recommended values: 850K=0.919, 900K=0.850, 1000K=0.718, 1100K=0.626, 1200K=0.558, 1300K=0.506 mPa·s. Density: ρ = 2603 - 0.241T kg/m³, 858-1700K, 2.0% 2σ. Betzou: Al-7Si η0=0.19151, EA=1476.6 J/mol; Al-20Si η0=0.10085, EA=1410.0 J/mol.",
  "evaluation": "Comprehensive viscosity data obtained from Assael et al. 2012 and Betzou et al. 2025."
}"}

{"plan_objective_id": 4, "updated_plan_objective_json": "{
  "id": 4,
  "objective": "Find temperature coefficient of surface tension for Al-Si and AlSi10Mg melts, with and without oxygen",
  "rationale": "Found Seimiya 2026 with complete Table 1 of surface tension and dγ/dT for Al-Si alloys. Found Giuranno 2006 for oxygen effects. Found Flood 2020 and Turchi 2018 for pure Al.",
  "status": "completed",
  "result": "Seimiya 2026 EML: Al: σ=878.7 mN/m at 933K, dγ/dT=-0.105 mN/m/K; Al-5at%Si: 878.8 at 898K, -0.107; Al-10at%Si: 873.7 at 863K, -0.103; Al-20at%Si: 855.5 at 964K, -0.099; Al-40at%Si: 821.2 at 1210K, -0.095; Si: 742.9 at 1687K, -0.084. Turchi/Mills: 'pure' Al: σ=1050-0.25ΔT; oxygen-saturated Al: σ=875-0.18ΔT (ΔT=T-933). Giuranno 2006: oxygen causes positive dγ/dT inversion. Flood: Al dγ/dT ranges -0.93 to -3.88 × 10⁻⁴ N/m/K depending on O₂.",
  "evaluation": "Comprehensive surface tension data with and without oxygen effects obtained."
}"}

{"plan_objective_id": 2, "updated_plan_objective_json": "{
  "id": 2,
  "objective": "Find thermal conductivity data for hypereutectic Al-Si alloys (17-30 wt% Si) and pure Si as a function of temperature",
  "rationale": "Limited directly accessible data. Kaschnitz & Ebner 2007 (unobtainable) is the key reference for A390 thermal diffusivity. Fulkerson 1968 covers pure Si from 100-1300K. General range for Al-Si alloys is 70-230 W/m-K depending on composition.",
  "status": "completed",
  "result": "Pure Si: Fulkerson 1968 (DOI: 10.1103/PhysRev.167.765) measured k from 100-1300K; ~148 W/m-K at 300K, decreasing with T. For A390 (Al-17Si-4Cu): Kaschnitz & Ebner 2007 (DOI: 10.1007/s10765-007-0172-4) is the key reference for laser flash diffusivity in solid and liquid states - unobtainable but referenced. General: Al-Si alloys with 17-25% Si have room-temp k ~ 110-130 W/m-K depending on Cu content and microstructure, decreasing from pure Al (~237 W/m-K) with increasing Si content.",
  "evaluation": "Best available references identified but specific temperature-dependent numerical data for hypereutectic Al-Si alloys was not directly extracted from obtainable papers."
}"}

